Does kube-prometheus-stack scrape Java application metrics?

By default: No.

It automatically scrapes Kubernetes components, but your Java application is not scraped unless you expose metrics and tell Prometheus to scrape it.

By default, it scrapes:
✅ Kubernetes API Server
✅ kubelet
✅ kube-state-metrics
✅ Node Exporter (CPU, Memory, Disk)
✅ CoreDNS
✅ etcd (if configured)
✅ Scheduler
✅ Controller Manager

For example:

Minikube
│
├── Node Exporter        ✅
├── kube-state-metrics   ✅
├── kubelet              ✅
├── API Server           ✅
└── Your Java App        ❌ (Not by default)
How does Prometheus scrape a Java application?

Your application must expose a metrics endpoint.

For example, with Spring Boot:

http://myapp:8080/actuator/prometheus

Then you create a ServiceMonitor (or PodMonitor) so Prometheus knows to scrape it.

Flow:

Java App
     │
     ▼
/actuator/prometheus
     │
     ▼
Service
     │
     ▼
ServiceMonitor
     │
     ▼
Prometheus

If you're using JBoss/Tomcat without Spring Boot, you can use the JMX Prometheus Exporter to expose JVM metrics.


s1:   helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts
s2:   helm repo update
s3:   kubectl create namespace monitoring
s4:   helm install monitoring prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack --namespace monitoring
s5:   kubectl get pods -n monitoring
      kubectl get svc -n monitoring

    o/p: pods running
        alertmanager-monitoring-kube-prometheus-alertmanager
        monitoring-grafana
        monitoring-kube-prometheus-operator
        monitoring-kube-state-metrics
        monitoring-prometheus-node-exporter

s6:   kubectl port-forward svc/monitoring-kube-prometheus-prometheus   9090:9090   -n monitoring --address 0.0.0.0
